# Lock shell scripts to LF regardless of the local core.autocrlf
# setting. Without this, a commit from a Windows checkout (autocrlf=true)
# rewrites *.sh with CRLF on commit; the Pi checks them out with LF and
# `git status` then shows them as permanently "modified," tripping the
# dirty-tree guard in update.sh and silently aborting self-updates.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same logic for any future text formats whose tooling assumes LF.
*.py text eol=lf
